3. Privacy and Local-Only Execution
The Software operates strictly locally on your macOS device. It does not contain network transmission capabilities, telemetry routines, or remote analytics. All cryptographic credentials and file state indices are stored exclusively on your local device.

4. Scope of Operation and User Responsibility
The Software provides in-place filesystem attribute and permission-based concealment designed to prevent casual inspection, inadvertent screen exposures, and search indexing. It does not perform destructive disk re-encoding or encryption containers. You acknowledge that:
(a) You are responsible for preserving your master password and offline Recovery Key;
(b) You should ensure backups of critical data before applying filesystem attribute modifications;
(c) The Software should not be used as a substitute for certified military or forensic-grade storage encryption.

